{#
  One free-text page (issue #368, ARCHITECTURE.md §8.116).

  Deliberately this short. A page is a title and a text, and the text is
  written with the site's ordinary configuration-mode editing — the same
  `editable()` the home page's introduction uses — so there is no form
  here, no layout to choose and no template to pick. The chantier is
  explicit that anything more would have left the feature's perimeter.

  `content_key` is `page_content_{id}` and is passed in by the
  controller rather than built here: keyed on the page's id, never on
  its slug, so a page that is ever renamed does not orphan its own text.

  The default is what a page that has just been created shows — a
  sentence saying it is empty, which a superadmin clicks « Modifier » on,
  rather than a blank screen that looks broken.
#}
{% extends "base.html.twig" %}

{% block title %}{{ page_title }} — {{ site_name }}{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
    {% include 'partials/page_header.html.twig' with { title: page_title } only %}

    {{ editable(content_key, '<p>Cette page n\'a pas encore de contenu.</p>') }}
{% endblock %}
